{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["T3", "T5"],
      "pins": ["T5.gate", "T5.drain", "T3.gate", "T3.drain"],
      "nets": ["ATO_VALVE", "PATO"],
      "observed": "On the ATO Valve driver (page 3, 'ATO Valve' block) the low-side switch on the PATO/ATO_VALVE net, whose gate is driven through R10 (100 Ω) from T4 (BT3904), is T5 = A03400A (a 30 V SOT-23 N-MOSFET). The AON6407 (T3) is instead placed in the power-train 'Reverse polarity protection' position (page 1), not on the valve net.",
      "expected": "The specification's component table assigns the AON6407 (T3, 8-DFN N-MOSFET) to the ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch: 'T3 — AON6407 ... ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch ... gate driven through R10 (100 Ω), pre-driven via T4 (BT3904).' The valve switch should therefore be the AON6407, not the A03400A.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Page 3 'ATO Valve': T4 BT3904 -> R10 100Ω -> gate of T5 A03400A; drain on PATO/ATO_VALVE net (sheet OPNhydro_r2, rev r2)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Page 1 'POWER TRAIN' under 'Reverse polarity protection': T3 AON6407 with R7 33k / D3 12V gate network (sheet OPNhydro_r2, rev r2)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "T3 — AON6407 (8-DFN N-MOSFET) | ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch | Netlist: drives ATO_VALVE net; gate driven through R10 (100 Ω), pre-driven via T4 (BT3904)."}
      ],
      "impact": "The two MOSFETs appear swapped between the valve position and the reverse-polarity position. The ATO valve is now switched by a 30 V device on a 24 V inductive load whose turn-off transients are only clamped to ~24 V by D4 and the 28 V TVS (D2), leaving little/insufficient Vds headroom; the valve driver can avalanche or fail, so ATO filling may stop working. (The reverse-polarity slot getting the higher-rated AON6407 is harmless.)",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The power, I2C, isolator, buck/LDO, current-sense and float/valve gate-drive sections all match the specification's values and topology, but the ATO solenoid-valve low-side MOSFET is an A03400A (T5) where the spec's component table specifies the AON6407 (T3) — the two FETs look swapped between the valve and the reverse-polarity-protection positions, an over-voltage-risk deviation from the intended design."
}

